# 4. A collection error fails the gate even when main has it.

# Given: a project whose gate command reports a collection error, both on the build's commit and on main.
# The test module imports a module that does not exist. kiln.json allows no round, so the first failing gate stops
# the build.

# When: a build reaches the gate.
exec kiln queue t
exec kiln run

# Then: the gate fails.
stdout '^t: stopped'
stdout '^  failing: `if \['
! stdout 'landed on main'

-- .kiln/kiln.json --
{"gate": ["if [ \"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\" = \"$(git rev-parse main)\" ]; then cp _junit/main.xml \"$KILN_JUNIT\"; else cp _junit/build.xml \"$KILN_JUNIT\"; fi; exit 1"], "rounds": 0}
-- .kiln/specs/t.md --
### 1. T is built

- **Given**: nothing.
- **When**: the gate runs.
- **Then**: the work is there.
-- _junit/main.xml --
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Written by pytest 9.2.0 under uv 0.13.7: tests/test_x.py imports a missing module. -->
<testsuites name="pytest tests"><testsuite name="pytest" errors="1" failures="0" skipped="0" tests="1" time="0.030" timestamp="2026-11-11T23:35:28.475475-05:00" hostname="localhost"><testcase classname="" name="tests.test_x" time="0.000"><error message="collection failure">ImportError while importing test module '/project/tests/test_x.py'.
Hint: make sure your test modules/packages have valid Python names.
Traceback:
/python/lib/python3.12/importlib/__init__.py:90: in import_module
    return _bootstrap._gcd_import(name[level:], package, level)
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
tests/test_x.py:1: in &lt;module&gt;
    import missing_module
E   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'missing_module'</error></testcase></testsuite></testsuites>
-- _junit/build.xml --
